# Dual-path architecture: unified pipeline + operations Ask LEO

> **Scheduled for deletion.** This rule only exists because the assertion
> vocabulary is copied by hand into nine places. Slice 3 of the pipeline
> refactor replaces those copies with one shared module, and this rule goes
> with them. Do not extend the tables below. Fix the duplication instead.

Post-processing layers (lab-value guard, scope guard, observable normalisation,
entity-type normalisation, value-unit linking, ConText, situation lookup, and
the disorder gate) are shared via `libs/pipeline/post_processing.py`
(`run_post_processing()`).  Both the training and runtime pipelines call this
single function.  Any change to a post-processing layer is automatically
applied to BOTH paths.

Changes to assertions, semantic tags, LLM prompt rules, or the escalation
flow still require updating BOTH the unified pipeline AND the Ask LEO /
escalation path, since escalation runs independently of post-processing.

## Unified post-processing pipeline (shared)

All layers live in `libs/pipeline/post_processing.py`. The table below is
**indicative, not complete**: 23 layers execute in
`run_post_processing_with_trace()` (count the `_run_layer(...)` calls), not 9.
The extra layers are lettered sub-steps such as `layer_2b`, `layer_3c`, and
`layer_7d`. Read the module docstring and the `_run_layer` calls for the real
order before you change anything.

| Layer | Module |
|-------|--------|
| 1 -- Post-Processor Rules | `libs/ner/post_processor_rules.py` |
| 2 -- Lab-Value Guard | `libs/ner/lab_value_guard.py` |
| 3 -- Scope Guard | `libs/ner/scope_guard.py` |
| 4 -- Observable Normalisation | `libs/ner/observable_post_processor.py` |
| 5 -- Value-Unit Linking | `libs/pipeline/post_processing.py` (`link_observable_value_units`) |
| 6 -- Entity-Type Normalisation | `libs/pipeline/post_processing.py` (`normalise_entity_types`) |
| 7 -- ConText Assertion Detection | `libs/ner/context_engine.py` |
| 8 -- Situation Lookup Normalisation | `libs/ner/context_detector.py` |
| 9 -- Disorder Gate (optional) | `libs/llm_client/disorder_verifier.py` |

